%table.idb-license-infographic-table
  %caption License options in Illinois Data Bank
  %thead
    %tr
      %th{scope: "col"}
        %h3 CC0
        %p CC0 1.0 Universal public domain dedication
      %th{scope: "col"}
        %h3 CC BY
        %p Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license
      %th{scope: "col"}
        %h3 Other License
        %p A license.txt file must be uploaded as part of the dataset files.
  %tbody
    %tr
      %td
        %h4 Derivative works are allowed
        %p Most open license with no restriction.
      %td
        %h4 Attribution is a legal requirement
        %p Partially open license with restrictions.
      %td
        %h4 Other CC licenses may create reuse difficulties
        %p
          CC NC, CC SA, and CC ND impose restrictions that may create incompatibilities and licensing difficulties for reuse of research data.
    %tr
      %td
        %h4 Request for attribution
        %p
          Attribution is not required, but creators can request citation or attribution information in dataset documentation.
      %td
        %h4 May create reuse difficulties
        %p
          Also known as
          %a{href: "https://web.archive.org/web/20160426155458/http://wir.okfn.org/2012/01/27/attribution-stacking-as-a-barrier-to-reuse/", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"} attribution stacking
          , which can become unwieldy in downstream reuse.
      %td
        %h4 Custom licensing considerations
        %p Writing a custom license requires legal expertise and non-standard licenses can complicate reuse.
